<section class="page-banner"><div class="container"><div class="section-label">ABOUT THE PLATFORM</div><h1>Connecting campus communities.</h1><p>An educational event and club management system inspired by the University of Vavuniya's student life.</p></div><div class="container" style="padding-bottom:35px"><p class="small-muted">Developed as a Group 17 IT2133(P) Advanced Web Programming student demonstration based on the group proposal submitted on 12 October 2026. The project is not an official university service.</p></div></section><section class="section container narrow"><div class="card panel"><h2>What is Vanni Campus Connect?</h2><p>This independent student software project demonstrates a centralized platform where students can explore societies, request membership, register for approved events and stay updated. Club leaders manage their communities; administrators review and moderate activities.</p><h3>How the platform is organized</h3><p>Browse <strong>Events</strong>, <strong>Clubs & societies</strong> and a monthly <strong>Calendar</strong>. After signing in, use your personal <strong>Dashboard</strong>. Organizers have a <strong>Club studio</strong>, and administrators have a separate approval and reporting area.</p><h3>Important disclaimer</h3><p>This is not an official University of Vavuniya service. University faculty and club names are used as public contextual references only. All demo users, events, memberships and notices are fictional unless independently confirmed. The official university name and emblem must not be presented as an endorsement.</p><p>For official information visit <a href="https://www.vau.ac.lk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.vau.ac.lk</a>.</p></div></section>
